# Input graph for
# mapsa__blathers__src_blathers_extract.py___extract_nested_node.
#
# _extract_nested_node(g, node) reads two patterns rooted at `node`:
#   * rdfs:comment (the trav_single_value site: g.value -> m{ }.first())
#   * every other predicate/value pair (g.predicate_objects -> m{ } loop),
#     grouped by predicate and filtered against _STRUCTURAL_NS.
#
# The driver resolves `node` itself, per call, from the same freshly-parsed
# graph (rdflib mints a fresh internal BNode id on every parse, so a literal
# BNode(...) here would never match) -- it looks it up via the named anchor
# triple ex:ClassA/B/C ex:hasNested _:nN.
#
#   * SEVERAL solutions, both patterns: _:n1 (anchored by ex:ClassA) has an
#     rdfs:comment AND four predicate/value pairs, including ex:label TWICE
#     -- exercises rows.setdefault + row.values.append growing one row from
#     two solutions -- plus a structural `a ex:NestedType` pair that must be
#     filtered out by _STRUCTURAL_NS (rdf: is one of its four namespaces)
#     without ever reaching _term_label for it.
#   * ZERO solutions for rdfs:comment -- the case that tells .first() (None)
#     apart from .one() (would raise): _:n2 (anchored by ex:ClassB) carries
#     predicate/value pairs but no rdfs:comment at all.
#   * NEIGHBOURHOOD that must NOT match either call: _:n3 (anchored by
#     ex:ClassC, never queried by the driver) has its own rdfs:comment and
#     ex:label -- proves the pattern is keyed on the exact `node` argument,
#     not merely on the predicate -- and ex:Other, a NAMED (non-blank)
#     resource with the same predicates, proving the read is scoped to a
#     blank node and not just "whatever has these predicates".
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

ex:ClassA ex:hasNested _:n1 .
_:n1 rdfs:comment "A commented nested node" ;
     a ex:NestedType ;
     ex:label "First" ;
     ex:label "Second" ;
     ex:weight 3 .

ex:ClassB ex:hasNested _:n2 .
_:n2 ex:label "Only value, no comment" ;
     a owl:Thing .

ex:ClassC ex:hasNested _:n3 .
_:n3 rdfs:comment "Must never be read" ;
     ex:label "Unrelated" .

ex:Other rdfs:comment "Also must never be read" ;
         ex:label "Also unrelated" .
